From: Langsdorff <131063968+clangsdorff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:12:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] camera: record samsung 60fps video modes behind
 persist.sys.phh.samsung.video60

the samsung hal keeps its 60fps video modes in its own video
configuration tags. when the prop is set, expose the 60fps ranges up
to the sizes the hal supports and force the requested fps range on
the request thread.

the hal only enters its 60fps sensor mode when the target fps rises
past 30 and loses it on every reconfigure, so after a reconfigure the
first request is capped at 30fps and the next one restarts the mode.
the hal also has no 60fps sensor mode outside 16:9, so sessions with
other aspect ratios stay at 30fps.

grapheneos camera has no frame rate setting and always asks for
30fps, so it gets forced to 60fps only when
persist.sys.phh.samsung.video60_grapheneos is also set.
